The in-turn rule (logcasts.ts inTurnStart) extended to two of the 14 overlapping ultimate pairs' obstacles, with its
other limits (the log quiet inside the moved stop, a move no larger than what it overlapped) kept:

1. A moved stop may overlap a third ultimate's by up to 3 frames (IN_TURN_FREE_FRAMES, the log's frame or two, as
   STOP_EDGE_MS allows at a quiet stretch's edges), tried after a start clear of every other stop: the chains of
   three, 3f78's Rossi (16.88 → 13.20 s, before Si's from 15.00 s) and d9e5's Gilberta (4.33 → 0.69 s, before
   Typhoeus's from 2.33 s).
2. The reach adds what the other stops (a teammate's combo slow-down) hold the landing's world frames by
   (IN_TURN_REACH_OTHERS): b6aa's Arcane (35.42 → 33.38 s, before Si's combo slow-down and ultimate).

Each pair it resolves leaves the overlap list (14 → 11, of which 5 are ≤ 4 frames).

Measured (2026-11-25, holds-and-placement round, freeze-ramp=runs, against 99806d9): development plain 68.1%
unchanged (3f78 damage −5.6 → −5.7%), hold-out unchanged, earlier pending plain 64.7 → 64.3%, mean |damage error|
4.1 → 4.7%: d9e5 plain 86 → 50, mismatch 7 → 20, damage 0.2 → 15% (Typhoeus's hits ×1.04 and her bursts ×1.22–1.25
from 10 s: Gilberta's ultimate 3.6 s earlier moves what it applies off the log's), b6aa mixed (plain 262 → 259,
mismatch 3 → 2, damage −5.5 → −4.4%).

Dropped: the logs say no. d9e5's opener (no logged hit before 2.33 s) reads as its three ultimates overlapping as
placed, and b6aa's move gains nothing. What would have to change: evidence for the d9e5 order beyond a quiet
stretch (the fight's start is quiet by itself).

